<ServiceLayout title="Arm and Leg Pain" description="Chiropractic treatment for arm and leg pain at Frey Clinic of Chiropractic in Napoleon, OH." schemaType="MedicalCondition">
<p>Pain in the arms or legs often originates not where you feel it, but in the spine. When nerves that exit the spinal column become compressed or irritated, they can send pain signals along their entire length — from your spine to your fingers or toes.</p>
<hr class="rule rule--accent" style="margin-block:var(--sp-6);" />
<h2>The spinal connection</h2>
<p>The nerves that control sensation and movement in your arms exit the cervical spine (neck), while those serving your legs exit the lumbar spine (lower back). A misalignment in either area can cause pain, numbness, tingling, or weakness in the corresponding limb — even if you feel no pain in your spine itself.</p>
<h2>Chiropractic approach</h2>
<p>By identifying and correcting spinal misalignments, we can often relieve arm and leg pain at its source. Our chiropractors perform a thorough evaluation to determine which spinal segments are involved and develop a targeted treatment plan.</p>
